% The markers take the accent; the text stays in ink. A marker is structure,
% not prose, and it belongs with the headings and the callout labels rather
% than with the words. The slides do the same, in the same way -- see
% \labelitemi in their ricardo-chrome.sty.
%
% Redefining \labelitemi and friends is not the shortest way to write this.
% enumitem has a font= key that styles a label and nothing else, so
% `\setlist[itemize]{font=\color{rzaccent}}' would colour every level of a
% list without naming a single glyph. That is how this was written first, and
% it works -- on LaTeX2e 2026-06-01, which is what the container runs. It does
% nothing on the 2025-11-01 that Arch ships, and neither does label= for a
% standard list: under that release's tagged-list code the label of an itemize
% or an enumerate is built outside enumitem's reach, so both came out in ink
% while subproblems, which enumitem owns through \newlist, came out blue. Same
% source, two LaTeX releases, two different documents.
%
% \labelitemi is read by both, so the colour lands either way.
%
% The glyphs are article's own, level by level, so naming them changes nothing
% about how a list looks -- bullet, dash, asterisk, middle dot, and 1. (a) i.
% Change one only to change the shape of a list. \theenumi is left alone on
% purpose: it is what \ref prints, and a cross-reference is not a marker.
\renewcommand{\labelitemi}{\textcolor{rzaccent}{\textbullet}}
\renewcommand{\labelitemii}{\textcolor{rzaccent}{\normalfont\bfseries\textendash}}
\renewcommand{\labelitemiii}{\textcolor{rzaccent}{\textasteriskcentered}}
\renewcommand{\labelitemiv}{\textcolor{rzaccent}{\textperiodcentered}}
\renewcommand{\labelenumi}{\textcolor{rzaccent}{\theenumi.}}
\renewcommand{\labelenumii}{\textcolor{rzaccent}{(\theenumii)}}
\renewcommand{\labelenumiii}{\textcolor{rzaccent}{\theenumiii.}}
\renewcommand{\labelenumiv}{\textcolor{rzaccent}{\theenumiv.}}

\setlist[itemize]{leftmargin=1.6em,itemsep=0.2em,topsep=0.35em}
\newlist{subproblems}{enumerate}{1}
\setlist[subproblems]{label=\textcolor{rzaccent}{(\alph*)},leftmargin=2.1em,
                      itemsep=0.25em,topsep=0.4em}

